sequenceDiagram
    title HAProxy and NGINX Ingress - Two-Layer Load Balancing Architecture

    participant User as 👤 User
    participant DNS as 🌐 DNS (/etc/hosts)
    participant HAProxy as ⚖️ HAProxy<br/>(External LB)
    participant Worker1 as 🖥️ Worker1:80
    participant Worker2 as 🖥️ Worker2:80
    participant Worker3 as 🖥️ Worker3:80
    participant NGINX1 as 🔀 NGINX Ingress<br/>(Worker1)
    participant NGINX2 as 🔀 NGINX Ingress<br/>(Worker2)
    participant NGINX3 as 🔀 NGINX Ingress<br/>(Worker3)
    participant Service as 🎯 api-service<br/>(Kubernetes)
    participant Pod as 📦 API Pod

    Note over User,Pod: Request: curl http://api-csharp.local/api/datetime

    User->>DNS: Resolve api-csharp.local
    DNS-->>User: 127.0.0.1

    User->>HAProxy: HTTP GET /api/datetime<br/>Host: api-csharp.local

    Note over HAProxy: Layer 1: Worker Selection<br/>Algorithm: Round-robin<br/>Health Check: /healthz

    HAProxy->>Worker2: Forward to Worker2<br/>(Round-robin selected)

    Note over Worker2: hostNetwork: true<br/>Port 80 listening

    Worker2->>NGINX2: Request arrives at<br/>NGINX Ingress Pod

    Note over NGINX2: Layer 2: Service Routing<br/>Check Host Header:<br/>"api-csharp.local"

    NGINX2->>Service: Route to api-service<br/>(Host match)

    Note over Service: Layer 3: Pod Selection<br/>kube-proxy<br/>Round-robin

    Service->>Pod: Forward to API Pod

    Pod-->>Service: Response:<br/>{"date":"26.10.2025",...}

    Service-->>NGINX2: Return response

    NGINX2-->>Worker2: Return response

    Worker2-->>HAProxy: Return response

    HAProxy-->>User: HTTP 200 OK<br/>{"date":"26.10.2025",...}

    Note over User,Pod: End-to-end latency: ~15-20ms

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
    Note over HAProxy,Worker3: Failover Scenario:<br/>If Worker2 DOWN → HAProxy routes to Worker1 or Worker3<br/>Health check every 2 seconds
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
    Note over NGINX1,NGINX3: High Availability:<br/>3 NGINX Ingress replicas (one per worker)<br/>hostNetwork: true on each worker
    end
